{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureShape","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureShape","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureShape.unit_total_gives_eighth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureShape.unit_total_gives_eighth","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SchwingerMeasureShape.lean#L81-L87","doc":"With the unit total (`c = 1`, one per-mode unit `a₀`) and the ½ split,\nthe per-channel measure is `1/(8π)` — the working coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureShape.efold_jacobian_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureShape.efold_jacobian_two","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SchwingerMeasureShape.lean#L70-L79","doc":"**The rival's arithmetic, pinned.** Under the Schwinger dimension\n`s = E⁻²` (the `E = m·c_q²` bridge), one energy e-fold is two proper-time\ne-folds: the log-measure Jacobian is exactly 2. This states the rival\nreading of the ½ precisely (adjudication vs the ρ-split reading: OPEN). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureShape.one_nat_per_efold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureShape.one_nat_per_efold","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SchwingerMeasureShape.lean#L60-L68","doc":"**One nat per e-fold.** In the logarithmic coordinate `ln t` — where the\nSchwinger measure `dt/t` is Lebesgue (`d(ln t)`; `∫_s^{es} dt/t = ln(es) −\nln s` by the fundamental theorem) — one e-fold `[s, e·s]` has measure\nexactly 1: with `k_B = 1` (nats), the measure's scalar is the nat-count per\nproper-time e-fold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureShape.scale_invariant_density_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureShape.scale_invariant_density_unique","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SchwingerMeasureShape.lean#L48-L58","doc":"**Shape rigidity.** A proper-time density satisfying the\nscale-invariance functional equation is `f(1)/s`: the Schwinger measure\n`c·ds/s` is the unique scale-invariant choice, up to the scalar `c = f(1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}